The '''2002 California gubernatorial election''' was an election that occurred on November 5, 2002. [[California Democratic Party|Democrat]] [[Gray Davis]] defeated [[California Republican Party|Republican]] [[Bill Simon (politician)|Bill Simon]] by 5% and was re-elected to a second four-year term as [[Governor of California]]. Davis would be [[2003 California gubernatorial recall election|recalled]] less than a year into his next term.

The 2002 gubernatorial primary occurred in March 2002. Gray Davis faced no major competitor in the primary and won the nomination. Simon defeated former [[Los Angeles, California|Los Angeles]] Mayor [[Richard Riordan]] in the Republican primary. Gray Davis ran a series of negative ads against Riordan in the primary. Riordan was seen as a moderate and early state polls showed him defeating Gray Davis in the general election.
