The '''2002 Ohio gubernatorial election''' took place on November 5, 2002. Incumbent [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] [[Governor of Ohio]] [[Bob Taft]] ran for re-election to a second and final term as governor, and he was opposed by [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] nominee [[Tim Hagan]], a former [[Cuyahoga County, Ohio|Cuyahoga County]] Commissioner. The race between Taft and Hagan was not competitive, and Taft was re-elected by a substantial margin, ensuring him a second term in office.

