The '''2002 Wyoming gubernatorial election''' was held on November 5, 2002. Incumbent [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] [[Governor of Wyoming|Governor]] [[Jim Geringer]] was term-limited and unable to seek a third term in office, thereby creating an open seat. Former [[United States Attorney|U.S. Attorney]] [[Dave Freudenthal]] and former [[Wyoming House of Representatives|Wyoming House]] Speaker [[Eli Bebout]] both emerged from competitive [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] and [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] primaries, respectively, and faced off against each other in the general election. Despite Wyoming's strong inclination to elect Republicans, a contentious race ensued, with Freudenthal ultimately defeating Bebout by fewer than 4,000 votes.
